      "content": "Wait, I'm a bit confused by your analysis. You're saying Witness A is preferred because he's more \"clear,\" but isn't it possible his professional appearance and certain way of speaking just make him *seem* more trustworthy to a jury, even if he didn't see as much? On the flip side, you mention Witness B carries a \"performative burden\" just because he was hanging out on the corner. Are you implying that his background or what he was wearing actually makes his testimony less reliable inherently, or is it just the way he phrased things?",
